The leaf/ directory is the upstream leaf crate, with these Mithka changes:
- Disable the bindgen/protobuf build script. Commit protobuf output and declare
  the two platform log FFI calls directly, avoiding libclang/protoc requirements.
- Exclude Android log paths from non-Android Apple builds.
- Permit system DNS without changing device DNS or routing.
- Expose embedded startup with pre-bound loopback TCP listeners and a ready
  callback. Listener failure ends that runtime; no UDP listeners are started.
- Support plain VLESS and the xtls-rprx-vision flow independently. Add streaming
  VLESS response/Vision parsing, a shared per-session read transition, and a
  TLS adapter that preserves record boundaries and avoids plaintext read-ahead.
- Compile-time feature gates support the selected protocols without pulling in
  unrelated protocols, TUN, API servers or a second cryptographic backend.
- Fix HTTP ingress header boundaries, bounded parsing, EOF handling, partial
  read buffers and CONNECT requests with pipelined tunnel bytes.

All original source files retain their upstream licensing. Root src/ and tests/
belong to Mithka's embedding package. Unsupported upstream features remain as
source for provenance but are not enabled in Mithka's Cargo.toml.
